{% comment %}
Stage 2 — one closed choice per (step, module the step was said to use): "which action of it?"

Only the modules stage 1 answered yes for are asked about, and a module with a single action is not
asked at all: with one option there is nothing to decide, and asking would invite a confidence score
about a foregone conclusion. Such a step's action is not a decision, it is a FACT of the module —
whoever assembles (step → action) reads it off the module rather than off an answer.

`criteria` is the closed set — the module's own action names. The decider picks one OF them rather
than producing a name, which is what stops an action being invented.
{% endcomment %}
{
  {%- assign sep = "" -%}
  {%- for s in goal.Step -%}
  {%- for m in modules -%}
  {%- assign key = "s" | append: s.Index | append: "_" | append: m.Name -%}
  {%- assign answer = moduleAnswer[key] -%}
  {%- if answer.noul >= threshold and m.Action.size > 1 -%}
  {{ sep }}"{{ key }}": {
    "type": "choice",
    "instructions": "`step[{{ s.Index }}].text` uses the plang module `{{ m.Name }}`. Which action of `{{ m.Name }}` does it call?",
    "criteria": [
      {%- assign asep = "" -%}
      {%- for a in m.Action -%}
      {{ asep }}{{ a.Name | store }}
      {%- assign asep = "," -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    ]
  }
  {%- assign sep = "," -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
}
